 is the Travancore Hindu Religious institutions act.\nTamil Nadu has a Hindu Religious and charitable endowments Department which works within the confines of Tamil Nadu Hindu Religious and Charitable Endowments Act- oversees all temples, muths, etc.", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-09-24T14:37:33Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "Will probe some more and get back when I have more clarity.", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-09-24T14:43:35Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "I mean all major religious institutions are ultimately controlled by the state govts. It’s a major sticking point for the free temples crowd", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-09-24T14:43:55Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "*the details of specific arrangements may vary", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]